    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "2. How to say 'I'll take it' or 'I'll have it'\n\nWhen you want to order a dish or buy some merchandise, you can use the following expression:\n\nJaa, sore onegai shimasu.    Well, then, that one please.\n\nThe word jaa means 'well (then)' and onegai shimasu literally means 'I make a request (for) ...' and is comparable to 'please' in English.\n\nIn place of sore in the above expression, you can use names of various objects or dishes. For example, when you want to order sukiyaki, you can say:\n\nSukiyaki onegai shimasu."
    }
